  "body": "Auction: 34 Shortland Street, City on Wednesday 18 November 2026 at 10:00AM  (unless sold prior)\r\n\r\nSecure. Secluded. Beautifully renovated. Exceptional coastal living.\r\n\r\nPrivately positioned down a driveway in a peaceful, secure setting, this beautifully renovated three-bedroom home offers an exceptional blend of privacy, contemporary elegance and effortless coastal living.\r\n\r\nJust a short stroll from Madills Farm, Tamaki Drive, the waterfront and St Heliers village, the location is simply outstanding.\r\n\r\nExtensively renovated with quality finishes throughout, the home showcases beautiful timber flooring, plantation shutters, skylights and light-filled interiors.\r\n\r\nA stunning entertainer's kitchen featuring premium Bosch appliances, bespoke cabinetry and Häfele fittings flows seamlessly into generous living and dining spaces. Bifold doors open to a sunny, north-facing courtyard surrounded by established greenery - perfect for relaxed entertaining.\r\n\r\nTwo separate living areas and two private balconies provide flexibility, comfort and peaceful spaces to unwind.\r\n\r\nProperty Highlights\r\n\r\n• 3 generous bedrooms and 2 beautifully renovated bathrooms\r\n• Secure, exceptionally private setting\r\n• Stylish kitchen with premium Bosch appliances\r\n• Two separate living areas and two private balconies\r\n• Sunny, north-facing courtyard\r\n• Beautiful timber flooring, skylights and plantation shutters\r\n• Double internal-access garage plus 3 off-street parks\r\n• Walking distance to Madills Farm, the waterfront and St Heliers village\r\n• Zoned for Kohimarama School and Glendowie College\r\n\r\nBeautifully renovated. Wonderfully private. Perfectly positioned.\r\n\r\nAn exceptional opportunity to enjoy stylish, low-maintenance living in one of Auckland's most desirable coastal neighbourhoods.\r\n\r\nFlexible viewing times available. If you need to sell or arrange finance before the deadline sale, please contact us.\r\n\r\nAll agent conjunctionals welcome and encouraged.",
